      "math_academy_id": "e-4023",
      "problem": "Express $2\\log_2(25) - 2\\log_2(5)$ as a single logarithm.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the quotient rule for logarithms:\n\n$$\n\\log_n(a) - \\log_n(b) = \\log_n\\left( \\dfrac{a}{b} \\right)\n$$\n\nIf we factor the given expression and use the quotient rule for logarithms, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{log}_{2}⁡(25)-2{log}_{2}⁡(5) & =2({log}_{2}⁡(25)-{log}_{2}⁡(5)) \\\\  & =2({log}_{2}⁡(\\frac{25}{5})) \\\\  & =2{log}_{2}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n2\\log_2(25) - 2\\log_2(5) = 2\\log_2(5).\n$$",
